  "details": "Follow up to previous post - issue now 100% determined. \n\n- Scaling a bone in y axis (along bone length) that is a bone for a physbone root transform will cause physbone Jitter. \n\n- This was introduced with the update that made boops public. Avatar was previously fine. \n\n- Tested on multiple bones (ears, whiskers, hair, tongue) on a fresh upload default Awtter avatar, as well as another avatars ears - issue was repeatable in both avatars. \n\n- It appears to be only the Y axis.\n\n- I have not tried negative scaling values. \n\n- physbone parameters not at fault. Impossible to get natural motion and eliminate jitter. \n\n- Jitter frequency is high in VR, and less noticeable in desktop mode. \n\n- See attached video of issue replicated on all root transform bones on Awtter.",
